.TH qsh-tunnel-close 1  "close 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-tunnel\-close \- Close a tunnel by id (`docs/CLI.md` §6.9, `tunnel.close`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh tunnel close\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fITUNNEL_ID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Close a tunnel by id (`docs/CLI.md` §6.9, `tunnel.close`).
.PP
Only ever reaches a daemon\-held reverse\-route (`\-R over reverse`) forward — a forward\-route tunnel\*(Aqs only "close" is its holding process exiting (`docs/CLI.md` §6.14). Idempotent: closing an id nothing currently holds answers `closed: false`, not an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fITUNNEL_ID\fR>
The `tunnel_id` from that tunnel\*(Aqs `tunnel.open`/`tunnels` entry
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
